---
// The client's Privacy Policy, supplied 21 Oct 2026. Wording changes go back
// to the client rather than being made here.
//
// Changed from the supplied text on 21 Oct 2026, at the client's request:
// - promotional use of project imagery now matches the Terms (used unless the
//   client opts out in writing), where the draft required permission first;
// - Google Analytics is named in the cookies section;
// - the contact email is the site's own inbox, CONTACT_EMAIL, not the
//   contact@ address the draft gave.
// The "updated" date moved with those changes, as the policy itself promises.
import {
  CONTACT_EMAIL,
  CONTACT_PHONE,
  CONTACT_PHONE_DIAL,
} from "../data/contact-info";
import LegalPage from "../layouts/LegalPage.astro";
---

<LegalPage
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="How Pixel Surveys collects, uses, stores and discloses personal information, including website analytics and aerial imagery captured during projects."
  updated="2026-10-21"
>
  <h2>Introduction</h2>
  <p>
    Pixel Surveys respects your privacy and is committed to handling personal
    information responsibly. This policy explains how information is collected,
    used, stored and disclosed when you visit pixelsurveys.com.au, contact Pixel
    Surveys or use its services.
  </p>

  <h2>Information We Collect</h2>
  <p>
    Depending on how you interact with Pixel Surveys, information collected may
    include:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Contact details:</strong> Name, email address, phone number,
      company and business address.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Project information:</strong> Site locations, project
      requirements, technical specifications and correspondence.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Aerial imagery and spatial data:</strong> Photographs, videos,
      maps, point clouds, terrain models and other data captured or processed
      for a project. This may incidentally include people, vehicles, buildings
      or neighbouring properties.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Website information:</strong> IP address, browser and device
      details, pages visited and other technical information collected through
      hosting logs, cookies or analytics tools, where enabled.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Information is generally collected directly from you or generated while
    providing services.
  </p>

  <h2>How We Use Information</h2>
  <p>
    Information may be used to respond to enquiries, prepare quotes, deliver
    services, process and provide project data, communicate with clients,
    maintain business records, meet legal obligations and maintain or improve
    the website.
  </p>
  <p>
    Information will not be used for unrelated purposes unless permitted or
    required by law, or with consent where required.
  </p>

  <h2>Aerial Imagery and Project Data</h2>
  <p>
    Drone operations and imagery capture are undertaken for legitimate project
    purposes, including surveying, mapping, measurement, inspection and
    monitoring. Depending on the project, imagery may incidentally capture
    identifiable people or information about surrounding properties.
  </p>
  <p>
    Reasonable steps will be taken, where appropriate, to minimise unnecessary
    collection and protect personal information. Project imagery and data are
    generally used to complete the agreed work and shared with the client or
    other authorised recipients.
  </p>
  <p>
    Unless a client advises otherwise in writing, Pixel Surveys may identify
    the client as a client and use project imagery and data in its portfolio,
    website and marketing materials. Confidential
    information, pricing and commercially sensitive detail will not be
    disclosed, and individuals and adjoining private property will be
    de-identified where reasonably practicable.
  </p>
  <p>
    Drone operations remain subject to applicable aviation, privacy and other
    legal requirements.
  </p>

  <h2>Disclosure and Storage</h2>
  <p>
    Pixel Surveys does not sell personal information. Information may be shared
    where reasonably necessary with website hosting and technical support
    providers, communication and business software providers, accounting
    services, professional advisers, authorised project participants, or
    government agencies where required or permitted by law.
  </p>
  <p>
    Information may be stored electronically through business systems and
    third-party service providers, some of which may operate overseas.
    Reasonable steps are taken to protect information from loss, misuse,
    unauthorised access or disclosure, although no electronic storage or
    transmission method is completely secure.
  </p>

  <h2>Cookies and Website Analytics</h2>
  <p>
    The website or its hosting and analytics providers may use cookies or
    collect technical information to support website functionality and
    understand visitor activity. You can manage cookies through your browser
    settings, although some website functions may be affected. Third-party
    services may handle information under their own privacy policies.
  </p>
  <p>
    This website uses Google Analytics, a service provided by Google, to
    understand how visitors use the site. Google Analytics uses cookies to
    collect information such as the pages you visit, how long you spend on
    them, your general location, and your browser and device type. This
    information is processed by Google, which may store it overseas, and is
    used by Pixel Surveys in aggregate to maintain and improve the website. It
    is not used to identify individual visitors.
  </p>
  <p>
    More information is available in{" "}
    <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" rel="noopener">Google&rsquo;s
    Privacy Policy</a>. You can opt out of Google Analytics using the{" "}
    <a href="https://tools.google.com/dlpage/gaoptout" rel="noopener">Google
    Analytics Opt-out Browser Add-on</a>, or by blocking cookies in your
    browser.
  </p>

  <h2>Retention of Information</h2>
  <p>
    Information is retained for as long as reasonably necessary to provide
    services, maintain project and business records, and meet applicable legal,
    contractual or accounting obligations. When no longer required, reasonable
    steps will be taken to securely delete or de-identify information where
    appropriate and legally permissible.
  </p>

  <h2>Access, Correction and Complaints</h2>
  <p>
    You may request access to personal information held about you or ask for
    it to be corrected. You may also raise a privacy concern using the contact
    details below. Identity verification may be required, and requests will be
    handled in accordance with applicable legal requirements.
  </p>
  <p>
    If you are not satisfied with the response to a privacy complaint, you may
    be able to contact the{" "}
    <a href="https://www.oaic.gov.au/" rel="noopener">Office of the Australian
    Information Commissioner (OAIC)</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Third-Party Websites</h2>
  <p>
    The website may link to external websites. Pixel Surveys is not responsible
    for their privacy practices, and you should review their policies
    separately.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes to This Policy</h2>
  <p>
    This policy may be updated to reflect changes to business practices,
    website services or legal requirements. The latest version will be
    published on this page with its updated date.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p class="contact-block">
    Email:{" "}
    <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a><br />
    Phone: <a href={`tel:${CONTACT_PHONE_DIAL}`}>{CONTACT_PHONE}</a>
  </p>
</LegalPage>
